From f763174bb47ce529c5fa6fdb7c5fda808f0ba05f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:13:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0209 -- ISR-replayed MIDI: pause is silent at
 once, resume continues the plan

WHY: in isr mode (0207) a pause only stopped planning: the up to 2 s already queued for the SB ISR
kept playing, and then the notes that had no queued note-off hung (PLAN.md follow-up 4). On the
main-loop poll a pause stopped dispatch at once (held notes aside).

WHAT: MidiPause calls SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(true) (SDL patch 0195): the replay holds, the queue is
kept, and every voice the replay left sounding is keyed off (OPL) / All Notes Off (MPU). Resume from
pause calls SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(false), which shifts the queued stamps by the pause's IRQs, and moves
the planner's slot position (and its last-seen IRQ) by the same count, so planning continues from the
slot it had reached and no song time is lost or skipped. Stop and song changes already silence at
once (0207: the planned-ahead writes are dropped and the sink's key-offs written out before the next
song's chip detection) and are unchanged. Requires SDL 0195.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nz9XeKeVG8Ab7dm8esJsMu
---
 Engine/media/audio/audioplayer.cpp | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/media/audio/audioplayer.cpp b/Engine/media/audio/audioplayer.cpp
index 9c144a23f..368679b58 100644
--- a/Engine/media/audio/audioplayer.cpp
+++ b/Engine/media/audio/audioplayer.cpp
@@ -474,6 +474,14 @@ void AudioPlayer::MidiPlay()
         }
         _playState = PlayStatePlaying;
         _midiResumed = true; // DOS-PORT (patch 0207): the next plan rebases, not "behind"
+        // DOS-PORT (patch 0209): the queue's stamps moved on by the pause's
+        // IRQs; move the plan with them so it continues from the same slot.
+        if (_midiIsr)
+        {
+            const uint32_t d = SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(false);
+            _midiPlanUs += (uint64_t)d * _midiPeriodUs;
+            _midiLastIrq += d;
+        }
         break;
     default:
         break;
@@ -508,6 +516,10 @@ void AudioPlayer::MidiPause()
     case PlayStatePlaying:
         _playState = PlayStatePaused;
         _midiPauseStartedMs = MidiNowMsRaw();
+        // DOS-PORT (patch 0209): isr mode -- silence at once and keep the plan
+        // (SDL patch 0195), instead of letting the ~2 s already queued play on.
+        if (_midiIsr)
+            SDL_DOSMidiDeferPause(true);
         break;
     default:
         break;
